  "context_pill": "Partial Integration of Agricultural Income",
  "example_summary": "This example demonstrates how to compute tax liability for Mr. X under the Old Tax Regime by integrating his agricultural income, comparing the impact of different basic exemption limits for ages 40 and 75.",
  "source_provision": "# Statutory Framework: Partial Integration of Agricultural Income\n\n### Master Statutory Summary Matrix\n\n| Provision / Mechanism | Statutory Condition / Limit | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 10(1) Exemption** | Income derived from agricultural operations in India | Fully exempt from Total Income; expenses incurred are deductible to arrive at Net Agricultural Income |\n| **Dual Threshold Test** | 1. Net Agricultural Income > ₹ 5,000 p.a.<br>2. Non-Agricultural Income > Basic Exemption Limit | If both conditions are satisfied, Partial Integration of taxes is mandatory under the Old Tax Regime |\n| **Step 1 Computation** | Aggregate Income = Non-Agricultural Total Income + Net Agricultural Income | Tax is calculated on Aggregate Income at applicable slab rates |\n| **Step 2 Computation** | Base Amount = Basic Exemption Limit + Net Agricultural Income | Tax is calculated on Base Amount at applicable slab rates |\n| **Step 3 Net Tax & Cess** | Net Base Tax = (Step 1 Tax - Step 2 Tax) | Add Health & Education Cess @ 4% on Net Base Tax to arrive at final tax payable |\n\n### Statutory Conditions for Partial Integration\n\n* **Applicability:** Applies exclusively to Individuals, HUFs, AOPs, BOIs, and Artificial Juridical Persons opting for the Old Tax Regime.\n* **Netting Principle:** Gross Agricultural Income is reduced by direct expenses incurred to earn such income before applying the ₹ 5,000 threshold.\n\n### Basic Exemption Limits under Old Tax Regime\n\n* **Resident Individual (< 60 years):** Basic Exemption Limit is **₹ 2,50,000**.\n* **Resident Senior Citizen (60 years to < 80 years):** Basic Exemption Limit is **₹ 3,00,000**.\n* **Resident Super Senior Citizen (80+ years):** Basic Exemption Limit is **₹ 5,00,000**.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Statutory Mechanics of Step Integration: Step 2 ensures that tax benefit is granted only to the extent of the basic exemption limit combined with agricultural income, thereby taxing non-agricultural income at higher marginal rates.",
